<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the hardened runtime has to be asked to allow. Every one of these is here because
  of how .NET and Silk.NET work, not as a precaution:

  - allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory: the CLR compiles IL to machine code at
    run time and writes it into pages it then executes. The hardened runtime forbids that
    outright unless it is asked for.
  - disable-library-validation: libs/osx-arm64 holds MoltenVK, GLFW, OpenAL Soft, shaderc
    and an FFmpeg build, none of them signed by the same team as the game. Without this the
    loader refuses every one of them and the game cannot open a window.
  - allow-dyld-environment-variables: the Vulkan loader is configured through VK_ICD_FILENAMES
    and DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH, which is how a player points the game at a Vulkan SDK they have
    installed rather than at the copy inside the bundle.

  Only meaningful when the bundle is signed with a real Developer ID, which is when the
  hardened runtime is switched on; an ad-hoc signature is not subject to any of it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
